      },
      "worked": "Draw radii from the incentre to the three points of tangency. Each radius is perpendicular to its side. At the right-angle vertex, the two radii and the two tangent segments form a square, so both tangent segments have length $r.$\n\nThe remaining segments on the legs have lengths $a-r$ and $b-r$. Tangent segments from the same vertex are equal, as follows from RHS congruence of the right triangles formed by the radii and the line to that vertex. Thus the hypotenuse consists of segments of lengths $a-r$ and $b-r$.\n$$\\begin{align*}c&=(a-r)+(b-r)\\\\c&=a+b-2r\\\\2r&=a+b-c\\\\r&=\\frac{a+b-c}{2}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
